# ⚠️ **This file's original reason is gone** — `output/` and `resource/` are no longer part of this project: both
# left the repository for the shared data root, namespaced `output/reel/` and `resource/reel/` (ADR 0007). This
# checkout's copies have been moved out, so these two rules are **inert here**.
#
# ⚠️ **They stay anyway, for a checkout that has not migrated.** A second clone still has the old folders until the
# one-time `mv` in `../../README.md` runs there, and in that window a bare `git add -A` would commit a master
# *song* — the one thing the reel's own `.gitignore` was written to prevent. Delete them once every checkout has
# migrated.
output/*
resource/*
#
# ⚠️ **`store/` still has no rule, deliberately.** It holds the recorded run that reproduces a reel — the same
# reason the brief commits its per-date snapshot. Machine state and rebuild evidence are not the same thing.

# Remotion's `public/` folder is staging only: the song is copied there for the duration of a run and deleted
# with it.
public/*

# The nested project's own environment and build noise.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.remotion/
.DS_Store
